# Send these one at a time, from top to bottom, while the API runs (dotnet run).
#
# Before you start:
# 1. Set @date to tomorrow, and @later to 9 days after @date.
# 2. Send the four logins below. From each answer, copy the "accessToken" and paste it after the
#    matching @ana, @mihai, @radu or @admin line. Tokens last one hour.
#
# The sample accounts all have the password Password1! and the ids ana, mihai, ioana, radu and admin.
# You can also try every request at http://localhost:5080/scalar: paste a token in the Bearer field.
# The database keeps everything between runs. The booking ids below are right for a new database,
# so to start over, stop the API and delete study-rooms.db.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@date = 2026-10-27
@later = 2026-11-05

@ana = paste-the-token-here
@mihai = paste-the-token-here
@radu = paste-the-token-here
@admin = paste-the-token-here

### Without a token: 401 Unauthorized
GET {{host}}/rooms

### Log in as Ana (200 with an accessToken and a refreshToken)
POST {{host}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana.popescu@example.com", "password": "Password1!" }

### Log in as Mihai
POST {{host}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "mihai.ionescu@example.com", "password": "Password1!" }

### Log in as Radu
POST {{host}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "radu.stan@example.com", "password": "Password1!" }

### Log in as the admin
POST {{host}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com", "password": "Password1!" }

### A wrong password (401)
POST {{host}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana.popescu@example.com", "password": "password" }

### Sign up with a password that is too short (400)
POST {{host}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "zoe@example.com", "password": "zoe", "displayName": "Zoe T." }

### Sign up (201). A second time gives 400: the email is taken.
POST {{host}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "zoe@example.com", "password": "Password1!", "displayName": "Zoe T." }

### Who am I?
GET {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

### Ana books A101 (capacity 3) from 10:00 to 12:00. People can ask to join, and she approves them (201)
POST {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "start": "10:00",
  "end": "12:00",
  "joinPolicy": "OnRequest"
}

### Mihai asks to join (200, "myStatus": "Requested")
POST {{host}}/bookings/1/join
Authorization: Bearer {{mihai}}

### Radu asks to join too
POST {{host}}/bookings/1/join
Authorization: Bearer {{radu}}

### Ana, the owner, sees both requests
GET {{host}}/bookings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

### Mihai sees the booking, but not who else is waiting
GET {{host}}/bookings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{mihai}}

### Radu tries to approve Mihai, but only the owner can (403 Forbidden)
POST {{host}}/bookings/1/participants/mihai/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{radu}}

### Ana approves Mihai (200, one place left)
POST {{host}}/bookings/1/participants/mihai/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

### Meanwhile Radu books B204 from 10:00 to 11:00 (201)
POST {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{radu}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 3,
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "start": "10:00",
  "end": "11:00",
  "joinPolicy": "Open"
}

### Ana approves Radu (409: he is in his own booking at that time now)
POST {{host}}/bookings/1/participants/radu/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

### So Ana declines him (200)
POST {{host}}/bookings/1/participants/radu/decline
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

### Mihai's bookings: the ones he is in or has asked to join
GET {{host}}/me/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{mihai}}

### Ana removes Mihai (200)
POST {{host}}/bookings/1/participants/mihai/remove
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

### A student calls an admin endpoint (403 Forbidden: logged in, but not an admin)
POST {{host}}/admin/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "C305", "building": "Library", "capacity": 4, "equipment": "Tv" }

### The admin adds the room (201)
POST {{host}}/admin/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "C305", "building": "Library", "capacity": 4, "equipment": "Tv" }

### Renaming A102 to A101 (409: the unique index on the name refuses it)
PUT {{host}}/admin/rooms/2
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "A101", "building": "Library", "capacity": 6, "equipment": "Whiteboard, PowerOutlets" }

### A class takes A102 from 14:00 to 16:00: a block, with no owner (201)
POST {{host}}/admin/bookings/blocks
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 2,
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "start": "14:00",
  "end": "16:00",
  "note": "Class: PCLP"
}

### Nobody can join a block (409)
POST {{host}}/bookings/3/join
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

### The admin books A102 for Mihai, more than 7 days ahead (201; a student would get 400)
POST {{host}}/admin/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 2,
  "date": "{{later}}",
  "start": "10:00",
  "end": "11:00",
  "studentEmail": "mihai.ionescu@example.com",
  "joinPolicy": "Open"
}

### What students see: display names, the block with its note
GET {{host}}/timetable?date={{date}}
Authorization: Bearer {{mihai}}

### What the admin sees: every booking, cancelled ones too, with emails and every participant's status
GET {{host}}/admin/bookings?date={{date}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### The admin cancels Radu's booking (200, the reason is ByAdmin)
POST {{host}}/admin/bookings/2/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### The admin removes A101 (204). The room is hidden, and Ana's booking is cancelled.
DELETE {{host}}/admin/rooms/1
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Ana's booking: cancelled, the reason is RoomRemoved
GET {{host}}/bookings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}

### A new access token, without the password. Paste the refreshToken from a login answer.
POST {{host}}/account/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "paste-the-refresh-token-here" }

### Two requests at once (from week 5). Set "DemoDelaySeconds": 3 in appsettings.json and restart.
### Then send this request and the next one within 3 seconds of each other.
### With the transaction, Ana gets 201 and Radu waits, then gets 409.
POST {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{ana}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 3,
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "start": "16:00",
  "end": "18:00",
  "joinPolicy": "Open"
}

### The second one, overlapping the first
POST {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{radu}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 3,
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "start": "17:00",
  "end": "19:00",
  "joinPolicy": "Open"
}
